Fillets: a walked blend whose contact on one face stands still while the
ball turns about it (mitcad#239).

Where a rounding runs past a corner that was rounded with the ball's own
radius (a box's vertical edge rounded with r, then its top edges with r;
the floor of a pocket whose inner corners are rounded with r), the ball's
centre stays on that corner's axis: its contact on the face across the
corner (the top, the floor) stands at one point while the other contact
sweeps round the corner. The blend there is the ball's own sphere, whose
side on that face is a point. Where the walk builds it (the faces are not
both elementary, so no analytic piece is made), the walk never set the
line's transition on the standing side (its contact curve has no
direction, BRepBlend_Line::TransitionOnS* threw Standard_DomainError in
StoreData or ComputeData), the standing side's twist flag was the sign of
numerical noise (the piece was then rebuilt as a filling surface), and the
orientation of the blend against the face was taken from the blend's
normal at the point side, which is null (StoreData failed).

- BRepBlend_Walking::TestArret: a contact whose tangent is below 1e-3 of
  the other's stands still; it is not twisted, and its transition is
  computed with the guide's tangent for its direction (the direction the
  contacts beside it on its face move).
- ChFi3d_Builder::StoreData: where the blend's normal at its side 1 is
  null (the side is a point), the orientation is taken with the normal a
  hundredth of the section inside.

The point side is then stored as 0171 stores the side of a ball turning
about the end of an edge (ChFi3d_FilDS): a degenerated edge of the blend's
face, no edge on the face.

Upstream: local to the walk's transitions and StoreData's orientation; a
moving contact is unchanged.
diff --git a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
index 46eeed6..bf10104 100644
--- a/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingAlgorithms/TKFillet/BRepBlend/BRepBlend_Walking.cxx
@@ -836,6 +836,32 @@ Blend_Status BRepBlend_Walking::TestArret(Blend_Function&    Function,
       {
         loctwist2 = true;
       }
+      // A contact that stands still while the other moves (the ball turning
+      // about it, where the other face is rounded with the ball's radius)
+      // has no direction of its own: it is not twisted, and its transition
+      // is the one it would have moving along the guide, as the contacts
+      // beside it on its face do.
+      const double vmax = std::max(V1.Magnitude(), V2.Magnitude());
+      if (!hguide.IsNull() && vmax > Precision::Confusion())
+      {
+        gp_Pnt pg;
+        gp_Vec tg;
+        hguide->D1(param, pg, tg);
+        if (tg.Magnitude() > gp::Resolution())
+        {
+          tg.Normalize();
+          if (V1.Magnitude() <= 1.e-3 * vmax)
+          {
+            V1        = tg * vmax;
+            loctwist1 = false;
+          }
+          else if (V2.Magnitude() <= 1.e-3 * vmax)
+          {
+            V2        = tg * vmax;
+            loctwist2 = false;
+          }
+        }
+      }
     }
 
     if (TestDefl && check)
